# grouped_type_unclosed_reject.tkr — the 9D-T1 (crumb 0019) unclosed-group reject anchor:
# `(A | B` in a type position without a closing `)` is a parse error, not a silently swallowed
# token.

Feature: grouped_type_unclosed_reject — an unclosed grouped type is a parse error

  Scenario: unclosed_paren_in_field_type_rejected
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "expected ')' to close a grouped type"
